                <pb facs="0623" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.1211 Laredo/42b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-10T11:00:00-05:00">January 10, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. For Clark. Situation at Laredo worse. Several of the banks seem affected. The
                    last thing we want to do is to bother you while you are working but I do want
                    you to know there is a really bad economic situation there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
